# cine act=setup fx="code:@place_pin;bg:meta_kings_chapel_river;x:.5;y:.45;go:researcher;lab:CAMBRIDGE UNIVERSITY;sub:Aleksandr Kogan's quiz · 2014;in:right;push:.018;pan:.005"
In twenty fourteen, a Cambridge University researcher named Aleksandr Kogan built a personality quiz called "This is your digital **life**."

// CARD a2-02 · SEE: NEW: a small square of gold dots, 270,000 DOWNLOADED; on "Through" it bursts into a field of blue dots that fills the frame: UP TO 87 MILLION PROFILES (FACEBOOK'S ESTIMATE) · SEAM out right
# cine act=rise fx="code:@cascade_field;bg:meta_art_scene_data_harvest;a:270,000;alab:DOWNLOADED THE QUIZ;b:UP TO 87 MILLION;blab:PROFILES · FACEBOOK'S OWN ESTIMATE;go:Through;src:about 82% in the United States;out:right;push:.008"
About two hundred and seventy thousand people downloaded **it**.
Through their friend lists, the app reached far more people than that.
Facebook's own estimate, published by its chief technology officer in April twenty eighteen, was up to eighty-seven million **profiles**.

// CARD a2-03 · SEE: three blocks rise on a dark floor: FIRST REPORTS 50M, FTC COMPLAINT 65M, FACEBOOK 87M; on "eighty-two" the note sets: about 82 % in the United States · SEAM in right
# cine act=doubt fx="code:@blocks;bg:stock_people_night_crowd_06;vals:50,65,87;labs:FIRST REPORTS · 2018,FTC · 2019,FACEBOOK · 2018;txts:50M,65M,87M;go:Other;gap:.6;in:right"
{wry} Other counts say fifty million, or sixty-five. Nobody outside the company has ever counted them **all**.
About eighty-two percent of those profiles belonged to people in the United **States**.

// CARD a2-04 · SEE: looking up at a real building on New Oxford Street, London; on "London" a name card drops at street level: CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA; on "Mercer" a second card drops high on the facade: THE MERCERS · Robert funded it, Rebekah on the board · SEAM out right
# cine act=setup fx="code:@landlord_tenant;bg:meta_coptic_new_oxford_junction;bot:CAMBRIDGE ANALYTICA^political consultants · London;top:THE MERCERS^Robert funded it · Rebekah on the board;botat:London;topat:Mercer;out:right"
Kogan passed the data to a political consulting firm in London called Cambridge **Analytica**.
It was bankrolled by the billionaire Robert Mercer, and his daughter Rebekah sat on its **board**.

// CARD a2-05 · SEE: a real phone feed, dim; two bars race: TRUMP CAMPAIGN 2016 to $5.9M, CRUZ CAMPAIGN to $5.8M; the source line: FEC filings · effect on votes disputed · SEAM in right
# cine act=doubt fx="code:@views_race;bg:stock_ui_phone_night_01;a:TRUMP CAMPAIGN · 2016;av:5.9;b:CRUZ CAMPAIGN · 2016;bv:5.8;max:7;go:Trump;src:paid to Cambridge Analytica · FEC filings · effect on votes disputed;in:right"
In twenty sixteen, the Trump campaign paid it five point nine million dollars, and the Cruz campaign five point eight million, election filings **show**.
Whether any of it changed a single vote is still **disputed**.

// CARD a2-06 · SEE: a receipt prints CERTIFICATION · DATA DELETED · SIGNED; on "check" a red stamp slams across it: NOT CHECKED · SEAM out right
# cine act=fall fx="code:@receipt_void;bg:meta_art_office_night;lines:CERTIFICATION~DATA DELETED~SIGNED;stamp:NOT CHECKED;go:check;sy:.5;src:Facebook · 2015 · users not told until 2018;out:right"
In twenty fifteen, Facebook found out where the data had **gone**.
It asked for the data to be deleted, and it accepted signed letters saying it **was**.
It did not check. And it did not tell the users. [BEAT]

